  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/03UJ">Remark <span data-tag="03UJ">64.16.3</span>.</a> Even though all we did are reductions and mostly algebra, the trace formula Theorem <a href="/tag/03UG" data-tag="03UG">64.16.1</a> is much stronger than Weil's geometric trace formula (Theorem <a href="/tag/03U1" data-tag="03U1">64.14.4</a>) because it applies to coefficient systems (sheaves), not merely constant coefficients. </p>
